9. On Line 152, oldValue stores the value of itemId 5 which is 20.
10. Line 155 updates the valueMapping with the newValue.
11. On Line 158, the check determines if the newValue is greater than the oldValue. Let’s divide this into two cases, one for upward heapify and one for downward heapify.

```solidity
File: MaxHeap.sol
150:     function updateValue(uint256 itemId, uint256 newValue) public onlyAdmin {
151:         uint256 position = positionMapping[itemId];
152:         uint256 oldValue = valueMapping[itemId];
153: 
154:         // Update the value in the valueMapping
155:         valueMapping[itemId] = newValue;
156: 
