description:
BaseRewardPool of Convex finance allows using mainly 2 different methods to get rewards one is:
```solidity
function getReward(address _account, bool _claimExtras) public
```
and other is:
```solidity
function getReward() external returns(bool)
```
as can be seen at #L980 - #L998 in the mainnet address 0x3Fe65692bfCD0e6CF84cB1E7d24108E434A7587e. The second one sets extra rewards to true by default. As it can be seen, the crv Reward pool sets extra rewards to false but cvx Rewards pool uses the second method here:
• ConvexDepositToken.sol#L284C1-L285C32:
```solidity
crvRewards.getReward(address(this), false);
cvxRewards.getReward(); //<@here
```
So the extra rewards are received by ConvexDepositToken.sol contract here. But the problem is it doesn't have a function to transfer out these extra rewards from the contract, similar to the one present in Curve Proxy as can be seen here:
• CurveProxy.sol#L255C3-L268C6:
```solidity
/**
@notice Transfer arbitrary token balances out of this contract
@dev Necessary for handling extra rewards on older gauge types
*/
function transferTokens(
address receiver,
TokenBalance[] calldata balances
) external onlyDepositManager returns (bool success) {
for (uint256 i; i < balances.length; i++) {
    balances[i].token.safeTransfer(receiver, balances[i].amount);
}
success = true;
}
```
Impact Explanation:
Extra tokens are withdrawn on behalf of ConvexDepositToken.sol, but there is no way to transfer them out causing them to be stuck on ConvexDepositToken.sol contract forever.

recommendation:
Either turn off the extra rewards functionality or create a function to withdraw those funds out similar to Curve Proxy

